// wheel_profiles.json - optional overrides for wheel/button-box naming, keyed by USB
// VID/PID. Loaded by Services/WheelProfileService.cs. Ships empty by default: nothing in
// this file is required for a wheel to work, it only lets you correct or add a friendly
// label without waiting for a code change and recompile.
//
// To add your own overrides without editing this bundled copy, create
// %AppData%/ECCR/wheel_profiles.json with the same shape - entries there win over anything
// with the same vendorId/productId in this file.
//
// Fields per entry:
//   vendorId   (required) - USB VID as a decimal integer (e.g. 0x346E = 13422).
//   productId  (optional) - USB PID as a decimal integer. Omit to match every product from
//                            this vendor.
//   name       (optional) - a friendly label for your own reference; not shown in the UI yet.
//   category   (optional) - one of: MozaWheel, LogitechRig, FanatecRig, ThrustmasterRig,
//                            SimagicRig, GenericWheelOrPedals, PlayStationController,
//                            NintendoController, XboxGamepad, GenericGamepad.
//                            Picks which hardcoded button/axis table this device falls back
//                            to for any index not covered below.
//   buttons    (optional) - map of raw button/POV index (as a string) -> display label.
//                            Indices 128/129/130/131 are the synthetic D-Pad Up/Right/Down/Left.
//   axes       (optional) - map of raw axis index 0-7 (X, Y, Z, RotationX, RotationY,
//                            RotationZ, Slider0, Slider1) -> display label.
//   xboxButtons   (optional) - map of raw button index (as a string) -> Xbox button name:
//                            A, B, X, Y, LB, RB, View, Menu, Guide, LSB, RSB. Used by Auto Map's
//                            "Xbox 360" and "Combined" layouts; buttons not listed stay generic
//                            "Button N". The D-pad hat is always bound as the Xbox D-pad.
//   axisRoles     (optional) - map of raw axis slot 0-7 (as a string) -> Steering, Gas, Brake,
//                            Clutch, Handbrake or Ignore. Default: X steering, Y gas, Z brake,
//                            Rx clutch, Ry handbrake.
//   invertedAxes  (optional) - list of axis slots that rest at maximum (typical for pedals).
//                            Omit to assume every pedal axis is inverted.
//   exposesXInput (optional) - true if Windows also shows this device as an XInput controller
//                            (its buttons then follow the standard Xbox order without an
//                            xboxButtons table). Auto-detected when omitted.
//
// Example (copy into your %AppData%/ECCR/wheel_profiles.json and edit to use):
// [
//   {
//     "vendorId": 13422,
//     "productId": 5,
//     "name": "Moza R9",
//     "category": "MozaWheel",
//     "buttons": { "0": "Wheel Button 1 (A / Cross)" },
//     "axes": { "0": "Steering" },
//     "xboxButtons": { "0": "A", "1": "B", "2": "X", "3": "Y", "4": "LB", "5": "RB" }
//   }
// ]
[]
